  "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
  "summary": "Ever since I was in middle school, I have been enthralled with computers and the programs they run. I asked others how they worked, but no one in my life was good with technology. It wasn't  long until 10 year old me discovered programming videos on YouTube. I watched video after video learning about the basics of programming. Throughout my time in middle school I was only able to learn the basics on my own. It wasn't until high school where I would gain the ability to develop full applications and software from scratch. In high school my engineering teacher noticed my passion for programming and helped me foster my love for it. He encouraged me to sign up for his AP computer science class where he taught me even more about programming. Together him and I founded the coding club for our school. He was a great mentor and teacher and I am forever grateful to have had him in life. My next discovery for my love of computer science would be in the University of Florida.\n\nDuring my time in UF I have worked part time for two clients. The first client wanted a website for comparing accident data between cities. I constructed the website with a few peers. I worked heavily on the API and algorithmic part of the project. UF provided the client as a means to practice software engineering. We used the opportunity to learn about agile methodology and the scrum framework. My second client was obtained through social networking. I and four peers were hired to build a website for a business he was creating. In this project I was the only member experienced in software development, none of my peers had ever used the required languages nor had they ever worked in a team before. Having realized this, I took charge of the team and was responsible for leading and managing the group. Using what I learned from my first client, I was able to set up a work environment that produced meaningful contributions within the first few days. By the end of the project the client was very pleased with the work we produced for him and asked if we wanted to continue working part time.\n\nIt was through the aforementioned projects that I discovered how much I truly love software development. Never have I felt more passionate than when I was working with a team. I started out my journey programming alone and limited in my knowledge, but now that I have discovered the wonders of teamwork, it has forever changed my perspective on software engineering.\n\nLanguages: C, C++, Java, Python , JavaScript, PHP, SQL\nCumulative GPA: 3.60\nCurrently working towards a Bachelor of Science in Computer Science",
